  "result": "I fixed it: subcommands now pick up the defaults set for them in `default_map`.\n\n**The bug:** when a context for a subcommand was created, it was handed the parent's whole `default_map` instead of the entry for that subcommand. So with `default_map={'sub': {'name': 'fromdm'}}`, the `sub` command searched the top-level map for a `name` key, found nothing, and fell back to its normal default.\n\n**The fix:** a one-line change at `src/click/core.py:392`. It now uses `parent.default_map.get(info_name)`, which gives each subcommand its own section of the map. This is also how upstream Click does it.\n\n**Checks:**\n- The full test suite passes: 1906 passed, 102 skipped, 1 xfailed.\n- I ran a small script with that `default_map`, and `sub` printed `fromdm`, the value from the map.\n\nI didn't add a regression test to the test suite; I can if you want one.",
